/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  totalReflux01_c6c7_yanagiRun628 -- the view the lesson opens on (DEV.md 4c C477).

  The lesson: at total reflux the column is pinned by the reboiler liquid
  (28.4 mol % cyclohexane) and the boil-up, and the ideal trays climb the
  cyclohexane profile further than the real trays of FRI run 628 did.

  The plot: the cyclohexane mole fraction tray by tray, liquid and vapour, on
  the ten ideal trays plus the reboiler.  The measured profile of the run
  (Yanagi and Sakata 1982, Table III: reflux 98.8 %, tray 10 97.4 %, tray 8
  93.7 %, tray 5 81.9 %, tray 4 73.2 %) is quoted in the case's flowsheetDict
  header, not held as a data file under constant/, so it is NOT drawn here: a
  parity or overlay against it needs a reference CSV, which no case file
  carries today.  The figure shows the model side only.

  This declares how the run is DRAWN, over what the column already publishes;
  it computes nothing and changes no number.  Grammar: docs/design/a-post-
  processing-dictionary.md.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

views
(
    {
        name    composition_by_tray;
        type    profile;
        title   "Total reflux, ideal trays: cyclohexane tray by tray";
        xAxis   { label "stage (1 = top tray, 11 = reboiler)"; unit "-"; scale linear; }
        yAxis   { label "cyclohexane mole fraction"; unit "-"; scale linear; }
        note    "Read it: the profile climbs from the reboiler's 0.284 to nearly pure cyclohexane at the top, tray by tray. The measured run (case header) had a reflux of 98.8 % cyclohexane and an overall tray efficiency of 70.8 %; these trays are ideal, so the column separates more than that run did, and the profile is the ceiling the real trays fall short of. The tray-by-tray measured values are in the header but not drawn here. The vapour leaving a tray equals the liquid on the tray above, which is the total-reflux operating line.";
        series
        (
            { name liquid; label "liquid on the tray"; unitOp column; table profile; x stage; y x_cyclohexane; style linesMarkers; }
            { name vapour; label "vapour leaving the tray"; unitOp column; table profile; x stage; y y_cyclohexane; style linesMarkers; }
        );
    }
);
